The other ways to turn on tracing: a separate -x after other options, set -o
xtrace, a shell started with -x, a shell: with -x, and xtrace in an env
value. set +x, set -o pipefail and grep -x are not tracing.
-- ci.yml --
name: ci
on: push
permissions: {contents: read}
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    env: {SHELLOPTS: xtrace}
    steps:
      - run: |
          set -eu -o pipefail -x
          set -o xtrace
          bash -ex ./script.sh
          /bin/sh -x ./script.sh
          set +x; set -o pipefail; grep -x ok out.txt
      - shell: bash -eux {0}
        run: go test ./...
-- want --
ci.yml:7 xtrace
ci.yml:10 xtrace
ci.yml:11 xtrace
ci.yml:12 xtrace
ci.yml:13 xtrace
ci.yml:15 xtrace
